      "last_updated": "2026-08-29T00:00:00.000000",
      "description": "What is the community made of, from kingdom down to class? Each ring is a rank (kingdom inside, then phylum, then class) and each arc is a taxon, its angle proportional to its relative abundance summed over the samples in view. Click an arc to zoom into it.\nHow to read: a wide arc is a dominant taxon, and many thin arcs under one phylum mean a diverse phylum. Hover an arc for its share of the whole and of its parent. Each sample weighs the same, since its abundances are relative.\nNote: no minimum arc share hides the rare taxa here, so the long tail of thin arcs can be hard to read; hover to read them.",
      "title_size": "sm",
      "title_align": "left",
      "use": "qiime2/sunburst_taxonomy",
      "catalog_source": {
        "toolId": "qiime2",
        "toolName": "QIIME 2",
        "outputId": "qiime2_sunburst_canonical",
        "use": "qiime2/sunburst_taxonomy",
        "description": "Hierarchical taxonomic composition (Kingdom\u2192\u2026\u2192Genus with relative abundance) for a sunburst, collapsed per sample from the QIIME2 per-rank rel-abundance tables."
      },
      "section": "Taxonomic structure",
